# SRG-APP-000100-AU-000730  -  CAT III
# The Central Log Server must generate audit records containing information
# that establishes the identity of any individual or process associated with
# the event.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000100-AU-000730
group:           V-221913
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-001487
control_rev5:    AU-3

contribution:    Every Splunk audit record names the account that performed the operation,
                 and those records reach a searchable index when the audit trail is queued
                 to the index.

governs:         audit.conf - The audit trail Splunk keeps of its own activity, and how those records
                 are signed.

check:           audit.conf [auditTrail] queueing not_equals false

external:        Shared or service accounts defeat attribution however the application is
                 configured; provisioning individual accounts is an organizational and
                 directory service responsibility.
external:        The identity field in each audit record is written by splunkd in a fixed
                 format with no configuration surface, so its content is confirmed by
                 inspecting a written record.

citation:        Three conditions removed. savedsearches.conf dispatchAs in user|owner is
                 the setting's entire permitted vocabulary - savedsearches.conf.spec gives
                 "dispatchAs = [user|owner]" - so it cannot fail and is not evidence; the
                 substantive value is "user", since "owner" runs a shared search "as if the
                 owner of the search dispatched the search, no matter which user requested
                 it", but the same spec notes that limits.conf
                 force_saved_search_dispatch_as_user = true resets dispatchAs to user, a
                 disjunction ANDed conditions cannot express, so it is left to inspection
                 rather than asserted wrongly. authorize.conf [role_<roleName>]
                 role_<roleName> present and props.conf [<spec>] <spec> present both name a
                 placeholder as a key that no such setting exists for; in their determined
                 form they are presence tests that every installation passes.
finding:         The audit trail is not queued to an index (queueing = false) with no
                 compensating input, so the account associated with each audited operation
                 is not searchable in the repository.
